# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does. File-level `!docs/openapi.yaml` works.

# CI and repo plumbing. .github/actions/ (the validate-catalog composite action) is
# consumed by other repos pinned to a release tag, so it is product.
/.github/**
!/.github/actions/
!/.github/actions/**
/.devcontainer/
/.claude/

# Agent / contributor docs (README* and examples/ are product on purpose).
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING*

# Tests and fixtures.
*_test.go
testdata/

# Linter / formatter / VCS config.
.golangci*
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.markdownlint*
.yamllint*

# views/ is the Vite/TS build source (build-time only). What ships is the committed
# internal/mcpserver/views/result.html, which is NOT under views/.
/views/
